<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" ><generator uri="https://jekyllrb.com/" version="3.9.2">Jekyll</generator><link href="http://localhost:4000/feed.xml" rel="self" type="application/atom+xml" /><link href="http://localhost:4000/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" /><updated>2026-11-06T11:53:23+01:00</updated><id>http://localhost:4000/feed.xml</id><title type="html">Siebe Vanlommel</title><subtitle>Not much here yet. This website is under perpetual construction. Perhaps check back later.</subtitle><entry><title type="html">Crane hunt part 2</title><link href="http://localhost:4000/2026/10/31/cologne.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Crane hunt part 2" /><published>2026-10-31T00:00:00+01:00</published><updated>2026-10-31T00:00:00+01:00</updated><id>http://localhost:4000/2026/10/31/cologne</id><content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost:4000/2026/10/31/cologne.html">&lt;p&gt;There’s a feeling I get, when I look to the West, except when crane migration is underway, which is when I am usually more fond of the East. For now, no significant eastern wind has blown any cranes off-track, so I was particularly excited to head eastward to Köln. Unfortunately, I learned that Köln lies beyond the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.kraniche.de/en/crane-migration.html&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;typical western migration route&lt;/a&gt;. Indeed, barely any cranes are reported over Cologne, although I am wary of the data, which comes from a user base heavily concentrated in Belgium and The Netherlands (see below, Source: &lt;a href=&quot;https://observation.org/species/19/maps/?start_date=2026-10-01&amp;amp;interval=86400&amp;amp;end_date=2026-11-05&amp;amp;map_type=heat&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;observation.org&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://opentopomap.org/about&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;OpenTopoMap&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;

