&lt;p&gt;Anyway, &lt;em&gt;Crane hunt part 2&lt;/em&gt; yields no sightings, however, Cologne was still a success, with 4 new lifers! First, in central Cologne, two parakeet species live: the &lt;a href=&quot;https://ebird.org/species/alepar2/BE&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Alexandrine parakeet&lt;/a&gt; and the &lt;a href=&quot;https://ebird.org/species/rorpar/BE&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;rose-ringed parakeet&lt;/a&gt;, the former of which is a new lifer to me. Their colourful presence feels off, and the pictures feel like they are taken in a zoo, because both parakeets are feral: descendants from escaped or released domesticated parakeets. Looking at it, it’s obvious that it belongs in its native colourful South Asian habitat and not in the drab streets of Cologne.&lt;/p&gt;

