&lt;p&gt;On Sunday, we took a hike in the Wahner Heide forest, which finally yielded the long-awaited sighting of the extremely cute &lt;a href=&quot;https://ebird.org/species/eurtre1/BE&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;Eurasian treecreeper&lt;/a&gt;. Very similar to the more common short-toed treecreeper, it has a lighter belly, shorter bill and a different call. Pics aren’t the best as light conditions weren’t optimal, but together with the clear sound bits I am confident this is a &lt;em&gt;certhia familiaris&lt;/em&gt;. Both occur in these parts, whereas this one does not occur in the western part of Belgium where I live. Going east was therefore not futile bird-wise.&lt;/p&gt;

