&lt;p&gt;Along the path there’s many great spotted woodpeckers foraging, goldcrests, nuthatches and robins. About ten minutes after the treecreeper success, Merlin indicates the possible presence of a &lt;a href=&quot;https://ebird.org/species/cretit2&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot;&gt;crested tit&lt;/a&gt;, the punkest of tits. We are able to find it but the best picture I manage to snag is not great, so I’ve also included the depiction of the &lt;em&gt;Haubenmeise&lt;/em&gt; from the information panel on birds of the forest. I have since taken a (slightly) better picture of a crested tit, which I’ll post shortly.&lt;/p&gt;

